  <!-- ============================================================
       TASKSET 5: MAP DISCIPLINARY INSIGHTS
       ============================================================ -->
  <Vertical id="homeless_taskset5">

    <!-- Recap: match insights to disciplines -->
    <Vertical id="homeless_insight_review">
      <Markdown>
## Match Each Insight to Its Discipline

For each disciplinary insight below, select the discipline it came from.
      </Markdown>
      <TabularMCQ id="hl_insight_review">
        mode: radio
        cols: Economics, Public Policy, Psychology
        rows: More job opportunities and labor-market flexibility are linked to lower homelessness, Greater access to TANF cash assistance is linked to lower family homelessness, Mental health disorders are highly prevalent among people experiencing homelessness
      </TabularMCQ>
    </Vertical>

   <IntakeGate ready="!@homeless_3_completion_page.value">
    <Markdown> </Markdown>
    <!-- Multidisciplinary map -->
    <Vertical id="homeless_insight_map">
      <Markdown>
## A First Map of Our Insights

Each insight explains one part of the problem.
      </Markdown>
      <Mermaid><![CDATA[
graph TD
    P[Homelessness]
    I1[Economic opportunity<br/>and labor-market flexibility<br/>—Economics] --> P
    I2[Access to income support<br/>—Public Policy] --> P
    I3[Mental health disorders<br/>—Psychology] --> P

    style P fill:#ffe1e1
    style I1 fill:#fff4e1
    style I2 fill:#fff4e1
    style I3 fill:#fff4e1
]]></Mermaid>
    </Vertical>
   </IntakeGate>

    <!-- Classify the map: multidisciplinary vs interdisciplinary -->
    <Tabs id="homeless_classify_map">
      <Vertical id="homeless_classify_map_t1" title="Classify the Map">
        <Markdown>
**Is this a multidisciplinary map or an interdisciplinary map?**
        </Markdown>
        <ChoiceInput id="hl_map_type">
          <Key>Multidisciplinary — each insight explains a separate part of the problem, with no links among them</Key>
          <Distractor>Interdisciplinary — it already shows how the insights relate to one another</Distractor>
        </ChoiceInput>
        <Markdown>**Explain your choice:**</Markdown>
        <TextArea id="hl_map_type_explanation" placeholder="I think this is a ... map because ..." />
      </Vertical>
      <Vertical id="homeless_classify_map_t2" title="The Map">
        <Use ref="homeless_insight_map" />
      </Vertical>
    </Tabs>

    <!-- Explain the connections between insights -->
    <Tabs id="homeless_connections">
      <Vertical id="homeless_connections_t1" title="Explain the Connections">
        <Markdown>
## How Do the Insights Connect?

For each pair of insights, explain how they might interact or affect one another.
        </Markdown>
        <Markdown>**Economic opportunity &harr; Income support:**</Markdown>
        <TextArea id="hl_conn_econ_income" placeholder="When economic opportunity is limited, access to income support matters more because..." />
        <Markdown>**Economic opportunity &harr; Mental health:**</Markdown>
        <TextArea id="hl_conn_econ_mh" placeholder="Job loss and economic instability and mental health may affect each other because..." />
        <Markdown>**Income support &harr; Mental health:**</Markdown>
        <TextArea id="hl_conn_income_mh" placeholder="Access to support programs and mental health may affect each other because..." />
      </Vertical>
      <Vertical id="homeless_connections_t2" title="The Map">
        <Use ref="homeless_insight_map" />
      </Vertical>
    </Tabs>

   <IntakeGate ready="!@homeless_3_completion_page.value">
    <Markdown> </Markdown>
    <!-- Integrated (interdisciplinary) map -->
    <Vertical id="homeless_integrated_map">
      <Markdown>
## An Integrated, Interdisciplinary Map

Adding arrows between the insights shows how they influence one another.
      </Markdown>
      <Mermaid><![CDATA[
graph TD
    P[Homelessness]
    I1[Economic opportunity<br/>—Economics]
    I2[Access to income support<br/>—Public Policy]
    I3[Mental health disorders<br/>—Psychology]

    I1 --> P
    I2 --> P
    I3 --> P
    I1 -->|fewer opportunities raise<br/>reliance on support| I2
    I1 -->|instability and job loss<br/>add stress| I3
    I2 -->|support buffers stress and<br/>stabilizes housing| I3

    style P fill:#ffe1e1
    style I1 fill:#fff4e1
    style I2 fill:#fff4e1
    style I3 fill:#fff4e1
]]></Mermaid>
    </Vertical>
   </IntakeGate>

   <IntakeGate ready="!@homeless_3_completion_page.value">
    <Markdown> </Markdown>
    <Vertical id="homeless_integration_summary">
      <Markdown>
## Summary of Interdisciplinary Connections

Homelessness is a complex problem with many interacting causes. Three disciplinary
insights help explain it, and they are connected:

- **Economics** shows that when there are fewer job opportunities and less labor-market
  flexibility, more people are at risk of losing housing.
- When economic opportunity is scarce, **access to income support** (a public-policy
  insight) becomes more important as a financial floor that keeps families housed.
- Economic instability and the experience of homelessness add stress and trauma, which
  connects to the **psychology** insight that mental health disorders are highly prevalent
  among people experiencing homelessness — and access to support can buffer that stress.

Taken together, these insights show that economic conditions, policy design, and mental
health interact over time, so an effective community response must address all three.
      </Markdown>
    </Vertical>
   </IntakeGate>
  </Vertical>

  <!-- ============================================================
       TASKSET 6: DEVELOP A PRESENTATION
       ============================================================ -->
  <Vertical id="homeless_taskset6">

   <IntakeGate ready="!@homeless_3_completion_page.value">
    <Markdown> </Markdown>
    <Vertical id="homeless_importance_unresolved">
      <Markdown>
## Is the Problem Important and Unresolved?

Repko's criteria also ask whether the problem is **important** and **not yet resolved**.
Draw on the community focus group and the studies you reviewed.
      </Markdown>
      <Markdown>**In your own words, explain why homelessness is an important problem that remains unresolved in this community:**</Markdown>
      <TextArea id="hl_importance_explanation" rows="5" placeholder="This problem is important because... It remains unresolved because..." />
    </Vertical>
   </IntakeGate>

    <!-- Presentation planning -->
    <Vertical id="homeless_presentation_plan">
      <Markdown>
## Plan the Public-Awareness Presentation

Anne Hastings has asked the team to share its findings with the community.
      </Markdown>
      <Markdown>**Who is the main audience for this presentation?**</Markdown>
      <ChoiceInput id="hl_presentation_audience">
        <Distractor>Academic researchers in a single discipline</Distractor>
        <Key>Community members, local leaders, and potential partners</Key>
        <Distractor>Only the Comm360 internal staff</Distractor>
      </ChoiceInput>
      <Markdown>**What are the key messages you want the audience to take away? (List two or three.)**</Markdown>
      <TextArea id="hl_presentation_messages" rows="5" placeholder="1. Homelessness has multiple, interacting causes...&#10;2. ...&#10;3. ..." />
    </Vertical>

    <!-- Presentation outline -->
    <Tabs id="homeless_presentation_outline">
      <Vertical id="homeless_presentation_outline_t1" title="Draft the Outline">
        <Markdown>
**Draft a short outline for the presentation that integrates the economics, public-policy,
and psychology insights into one coherent story about the causes of homelessness.**
        </Markdown>
        <TextArea id="hl_presentation_outline" rows="10" placeholder="Slide 1: The problem...&#10;Slide 2: What the community told us...&#10;Slide 3: What the research shows (economics, policy, mental health)...&#10;Slide 4: How the causes connect...&#10;Slide 5: What Comm360 can do..." />
      </Vertical>
      <Vertical id="homeless_presentation_outline_t2" title="Integrated Summary">
        <Use ref="homeless_integration_summary" />
      </Vertical>
    </Tabs>
  </Vertical>

   <!-- Completion summary -->
  <Vertical id="completion_homeless_3">
  <CheckboxInput id="homeless_3_completion_page">
    <Markdown id="homeless_3_confirmation">**Confirm that you are done with this exercise.**</Markdown>
    <Key id="Homeless_Part_3_finished">I don't need to make any more changes</Key>
  </CheckboxInput>
  <IntakeGate ready="'Homeless_Part_3_finished' in @homeless_3_completion_page.value">
   <Markdown> </Markdown>
   <Markdown>
## Part 3 Complete!

### What you accomplished across the three parts:

1. **Brainstormed** individual-level and structural causes of homelessness
2. **Reviewed** community focus-group data and selected focus areas
3. **Reflected** on whether homelessness is an interdisciplinary problem
4. **Reviewed the literature** from economics, public policy, and psychology
5. **Mapped and integrated** the disciplinary insights
6. **Developed a presentation** to share the findings with the community

## PLEASE CLICK CONTINUE TO REVIEW YOUR RESPONSES AND SAVE THEM TO A PDF. THEN UPLOAD THE PDF TO YOUR COURSE SYSTEM.
     </Markdown>
   </IntakeGate>
